      "content": "I'll read both the original test and the CUT to understand the code before improving understandability.Now I have a clear picture. The test checks `lookupDegreesSizeForHashLen` for odd (3) and even (4) length hashes. The array returned is `[latHeight, lonWidth]` — but the original code uses opaque names like `boxOdd[0]`/`boxOdd[1]` with no explanation. I'll improve understandability by:\n\n1. Removing the unused `SpatialContext ctx` field\n2. Renaming variables to express their meaning (`oddLengthDegrees`, `evenLengthDegrees`)\n3. Extracting named variables for the result indices (`latHeight`, `lonWidth`)\n4. Adding concise, meaningful comments\n5. Extracting the delta tolerance as a named constantNow I'll compile-check the generated test.The improved test compiled successfully — all understandability changes are syntactically and symbolically correct against the CUT."
